The Western blot in Fig. 7D illustrates the processing and secretion of IL-1β by dendritic cells. A ~30kD band, corresponding to pro-IL-1β, is observed in cell lysates when cells are primed with LPS. In the supernatant, a ~15kD band, representing the active secreted IL-1β (which is typically 17kD), is prominent when cells are primed with LPS and stimulated with Nano-11, indicating Nano-11 promotes the cleavage and release of active IL-1β.